			},
			"date": "2026-02-07T13:59:06.971Z",
			"content": "<p>I mean, this is to mitigate the usual hack of people doing this:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://example.com\">google.com</a></p>\n<p>The modal only pops up if the domain in the hyperlink facet doesn't match the text its decorating. Its a fairly usual mitigation against such an attack, and I've seen it in a few other apps (Telegram springs to mind too)</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
